The blank-key control is placed before the download on purpose: refusing *after* fetching 150 MB would
still be a refusal, but it would not prove the key is validated up front, which is the property that
keeps a mistaken environment variable from spending the bandwidth and half-writing a store. The foreign-
key control is the opposite half -- a key that parses as a valid Ed25519 key but did not sign this build
must be refused by the signature check, not by the parse, and the transcript shows the checksum passing
first and the signature line refusing after it. The third control in that section is the one that makes
the other two worth reading: the refused install left the artifact already in the store at the same
digest, so a failed control run does not poison the machine for the next one.

Cross-checks after the run:

- `gh release list` still reports `v0.4.2` as latest (published 2026-09-23T13:18:43Z), so the version
  the lab installed is still the newest published one; the repository is ahead of it, unchanged from
  the section above.
- The digest the installer checked (`0ee7d6ee3c92159d2b013c7d081cf2cc265d2d59a808ebb0fb9f2554a7b4bfa2`)
  is the same one recorded on 2026-10-02 and the same one in
  `docs/verification/release-signature-v0.4.2-2026-10-02.log`, i.e. the published artifact has not been
  re-uploaded underneath these transcripts.
- `cmp` on the published raw `main` copy versus the tree copy: identical (the lab asserts the same thing
  from inside the container, before it runs the installer).

What this re-run does NOT change: every limit in "What this file is NOT evidence about" still applies
unchanged -- `install.ps1` and `install.bat` have still never been executed, no macOS or arm64, mirrors
and `CHAOS_CN=1` untouched, `CHAOS_SKIP_CHECKSUM`/`CHAOS_SKIP_SIGNATURE` unexercised, no upgrade across
differing versions, and the escape hatches are asserted absent rather than tested present.

`scripts/install.sh` has not been touched since that run: `git log --oneline -1 -- scripts/install.sh`
still names `88511413`, and `cmp` of the file at `1487aded` against the file at `ef33dfd9` (the head
pushed on 2026-10-03) reports no difference. So this transcript still describes the installer that is
on `main`, and no re-run is owed for the commits since.


